# Numerical witnesses for the native/saved Hermitian comparison

The change of basis permutes the 22 point blocks and applies the same binary
nine-by-nine matrix in each fiber. Columns are packed as natural numbers,
with bit zero the first row. `SavedComparison` checks these witnesses against
the literal native correction words and the unchanged saved generator data.
The adjacent discovery script solves the intertwining equations over F₂;
its output is used only as a witness, never as a proof oracle.

Source context: Guralnick--Malle I, Proposition 5.1, pp.15--16;
Aschbacher--Smith, printed pp.451--452,457.
-/

